-- Restore variant words the source file dropped from 84 perfume names and concentrations.
--
-- The source kept words such as "Intense" only at the end of the Parfumo address: the row at
-- .../Azzaro_pour_Homme_Eau_de_Toilette_Intense is named "Azzaro pour Homme", "Eau de Toilette",
-- so the flanker appeared under its base perfume's name, with the flanker's notes and year. 11 of
-- these rows are in the puzzle pool (is_uncertain = false); none has been a daily puzzle yet
-- (checked 2026-11-26). The ETL now restores the same words on import (scripts/etl.py,
-- restore_variant); this list comes from that function run on the 2026-11 source file, so a later
-- import matches these rows by their new key instead of adding copies.
--
-- Rows keep their ids (game history and image assets stay attached). source_record_slug and the
-- fingerprints are the values the ETL computes for the restored name; the unique_slug trigger
-- recomputes unique_slug. Eleven source rows whose variant collided with their base row on the old
-- key are left to the next import, which adds the variant as its own row.
--
-- Non-ASCII characters are written as U& escapes so the file stays ASCII.

-- The view refresh takes an exclusive lock on perfume_autocomplete_cache (about 59 000 rows):
-- give up rather than queue behind a long reader, and bound the whole migration.
SET lock_timeout = '5s';
SET statement_timeout = '60s';

-- Concentration names and slugs as the ETL creates them (slugify); existing ones stay.
